<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<templates id="template" xml:space="preserve">

    <!--
        Phase 6 — Receipt lot/serial display.

        ODOO 18 NOTE:
        Odoo 18 renders Lot/Serial numbers on the printed receipt NATIVELY:
        each orderline's getDisplayData() returns `packLotLines`, and the core
        `point_of_sale.Orderline` template prints them
        (<li t-foreach="line.packLotLines or []" ...>).

        The previous custom extension inherited `point_of_sale.OrderReceipt`
        and referenced `order.config`. In Odoo 18 the receipt template has NO
        `order` variable in scope (it renders from `props.data` only), so that
        reference threw "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'config')"
        and crashed the receipt / payment screen.

        Since core already shows the lots, no extension is needed on Odoo 18.
        This file is intentionally a no-op (kept so the assets glob stays
        stable across phases).
    -->

</templates>
